WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.750
This is the Singularity Daily, for Tuesday, November 10.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.930
Here are the last 24 hours in superintelligence, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.230
Today's about bouncing back.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:21.990
ChatGPT's growth is climbing again: 81% of chatbot traffic.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:25.460
Markets bounced too. Asian tech stocks rose Monday,

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.750
and so did chipmakers like Intel.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.570
In China,

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:38.950
DeepSeek's agent app Harness passed 1.5 million daily users in under three months.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.880
Disney's teaming up with Adobe to build AI

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.550
models trained on its characters and worlds.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.040
Musk says you could wish for a castle,

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.740
and superintelligence would make it on the side.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.600
Instagram's AI age-guesser goes worldwide,

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.230
hunting for teens who claim to be adults.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:06.190
Meanwhile, Nvidia's board is investigating its boss's ties to an alleged Chinese spy.

00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:07.350
Shares fell 5%.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.290
President Trump stood by him: "an honorable guy," he said,

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:13.190
who's done "an amazing job."

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.080
And Google picked this week to unveil two new versions of its AI chips,

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:20.060
aimed at Nvidia.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.800
Bloomberg's analysts see its chip sales topping $135 billion by 2028.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.710
Chinese scientists made comfy brain-reading electrodes that topped 94% at mind-typing,

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:36.640
all day long.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.190
And MIT built one AI model that simulates sliding sand,

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:43.750
sloshing fluids and folding proteins.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.230
The catch? Regulators say Waymo kept passing stopped school buses after its fix.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:56.000
And about 1,100 Claude Code files on GitHub were leaking passwords and keys.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.690
Apple researchers put a Mac mini on a robot,

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:07.380
and it navigated rooms it had never seen.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:14.790
Tesla opened its robotaxis to San Antonio at 5 a.m. Monday, another Texas city.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:21.350
In Lisbon, robots are official speakers at Web Summit for the very first time.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.690
Everyone stumbles sometimes. The ones we remember are the ones who bounce back.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.030
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.780
Somehow, the future keeps landing early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.370
That's one day of news. Imagine what a year looks like.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Singularity Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.120
Same time tomorrow?

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.010
Want the whole month? Hear more on November 27.
